WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.645
A control limit sees one point at a time. The

2
00:00:03.745 --> 00:00:07.973
Western Electric rules read the run, so the chart is

3
00:00:08.073 --> 00:00:11.636
divided into one, two and three sigma zones.

4
00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:15.367
Forty subgroups from a process that looks calm at

5
00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:19.025
a glance. Only one point ever leaves the limits.

6
00:00:19.116 --> 00:00:24.296
Rule one: point beyond 3 sigma. Subgroup 11.

7
00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:31.243
Rule two: 2 of 3 beyond 2 sigma, same side. Subgroup 16.

8
00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:38.025
Rule three: 4 of 5 beyond 1 sigma, same side. Subgroup 24.

9
00:00:38.116 --> 00:00:43.728
Rule four: 8 in a row, same side. Subgroup 32.

10
00:00:43.816 --> 00:00:48.882
The last one is the point of the whole idea. Eight subgroups in a row

11
00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:53.748
on one side of centre, and not one of them anywhere near a limit.

12
00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:57.039
A shift too small to breach a limit still shows up

13
00:00:57.139 --> 00:01:00.213
in the pattern, which is what the rules are for.

